### 逐处错误标注
1. has been → has become  表达 “成为一种现象” 用 become 更贴合四级写作习惯
2. the ability of considering → the ability to consider 固定搭配：the ability to do sth.
3. instead of help → instead of helping  of 是介词，后面接动名词
4. learn positively to cooperate → learn to cooperate properly 语序和用词不当，positively 此处不合适
5. AI could assist → AI can assist 全文为一般现在时陈述普遍现象，不用 could
6. assist them with scheduling their studying plans → assist them in scheduling their study plans 固定搭配 assist sb. in doing；study plans 为常用表达，不用 studying plans
7. student → students 泛指，用复数
8. use properly AI tools → use AI tools properly 副词修饰动词，放在宾语之后
9. be better and better → make steady progress 表达更地道，四级作文加分表达

### 修正版
  Nowadays, using AI tools has become a common phenomenon. Opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, students are supposed to use AI tools within limits.
  On the one hand, if students over-rely on AI tools to finish their school tasks, they may gradually lose the ability to consider and handle problems independently. AI tools 
should help students improve their academic performance instead of helping them escape their tasks. On the other hand, students should learn to cooperate with AI tools properly. 
For example, AI can assist them in scheduling their study plans and offering useful tips.
  From my perspective, students should use AI tools properly to elevate their academic performance and thinking abilities. Only in this way can students make steady progress.

### 优化完整版
  Nowadays, using AI tools has become a common phenomenon. Opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, students are supposed to use AI tools within reasonable 
limits.
  On the one hand, over-reliance on AI to complete school assignments will deprive students of the chance to think independently. If they simply copy answers generated by AI, 
they can hardly master knowledge and develop problem-solving skills. On the other hand, AI is a helpful auxiliary tool. It can sort out learning materials and offer practical 
suggestions for review, greatly improving learning efficiency.
  From my perspective, we should treat AI as a learning assistant rather than a substitute for independent thinking. Only in this way can we make the most of AI and achieve real
progress in our studies.
